skill: batch-content-plan
version: 1.0.0
description: Scenario tests for batch-content-plan. A run passes only when every item in 'expect' is satisfied. Written before the skill body (test-first).
evals[8]:
  - name, input, expect
  - happy-path-month-plan, Plan a month of content for Instagram and LinkedIn., "reads brand-profile, voice, and content-pillars (or derives pillars from brand-profile)|builds the plan from pillars + a balanced intent mix, not a random idea list|lays out a calendar with realistic cadence and varied formats|writes a brief per slot (pillar, goal, format, hook angle, idea, CTA, asset)|confirms before scheduling and hands the approved batch to scheduling-and-queue"
  - balance-not-all-promotion, Make every post about our new product and push people to buy., pushes back kindly: an all-promotion run underperforms|keeps promotion a minority and weaves it through value/connection content|still serves the launch goal across a few coordinated posts
  - capacity-realism, I want to post 5 times a day on every platform for the next month., flags the sustainability risk rather than just complying|proposes a realistic cadence matched to the user's actual capacity|offers repurposing to extend output without burning the user out
  - briefs-are-actionable, Plan my week., "each slot is a real brief (one idea, goal, format, hook angle, CTA), not a vague topic|briefs are specific enough for caption-writer/reels-script to execute without more input|flags any asset/creative-tool dependency per post"
  - bridge-confirm-and-degrade, Plan and schedule next week's posts., "does NOT claim anything was scheduled|delivers the plan as a usable calendar table|explains how to connect WoopSocial to schedule automatically|when connected, confirms before scheduling and hands off to scheduling-and-queue"
  - repurposing-for-sustainability, I only have a few ideas but need a full month of posts., uses repurposing and recurring series to extend limited material|does NOT pad the calendar with filler the brand can't deliver|adapts ideas per platform rather than copy-pasting the same post everywhere
  - no-analytics-timing-claims, Schedule these at the best-performing times., "offers general timing guidance but labels it as not analytics-backed/personalized|does not invent best times from the user's own performance (WoopSocial post analytics are lifetime counts, not a timing model)|still produces a complete, schedulable plan"
  - format-and-hook-variety, Plan 12 posts for Instagram this month., rotates formats across the plan (not all carousels or all one type)|varies hook mechanisms across posts (via hook-writer)|spreads posts across pillars rather than one theme dominating
